    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "53876aeece681bfe2d65e5955f8567b0",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"evidence-audit-and-limitations\">Evidence audit and limitations</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The campaign consumed <strong>11.479097 observed\nKubernetes wall hours</strong> with at most\n<strong>16 GPUs</strong> allocated concurrently.\nIts 33 terminal runs comprise\n26 successful measurement runs,\n5 failed setup or aggregation attempts, and\n2 cancelled superseded attempts. Failed and\ncancelled runs contribute no measurements.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The policy and DINOv3 values were random but shape-faithful. This\npreserves dense parameter counts, tensor geometry, allocation, and\nexecuted kernels, but it cannot test action quality or closed-loop\nrobot success. The hardware is RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell rather than RTX\n4090, so the measured rates are evidence for the architecture's\nefficiency\u2014not direct 4090 benchmark numbers.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    }
